# i18n Patterns

## Supported Languages
- English (`en`)
- Spanish (`es`)
- Traditional Chinese (`zh-TW`)

## Server-Side i18n

### Always Use `getServerTranslations()`

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Correct function
import { getServerTranslations } from '@/lib/i18n/server'

export default async function Page() {
  const { locale, translations } = await getServerTranslations()
  return <h1>{translations.home.title}</h1>
}

// ❌ BAD - Function doesn't exist
import { getServerLocale } from '@/lib/i18n/server' // ERROR: Not exported!
```

## MDX Content Structure

All blog posts must have 3 language versions:

```
content/blog/bitcoin-whitepaper-explained/
  index.mdx        # English
  index.es.mdx     # Spanish
  index.zh-TW.mdx  # Traditional Chinese
```

### MDX Frontmatter

```yaml
---
title: "Article Title"
slug: "article-slug"
date: "2026-01-22"
description: "Article description"
readingTime: 15
category: "Blockchain"
tags: ["bitcoin", "blockchain"]
featured: false
---
```

## JSON Configuration Files

For learning paths and other structured content:

```json
{
  "title": {
    "en": "English Title",
    "es": "Spanish Title",
    "zh-TW": "Traditional Chinese Title"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "English description",
    "es": "Spanish description",
    "zh-TW": "Traditional Chinese description"
  }
}
```

## Getting Localized Text

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Safe accessor with fallback
const title = track.title[locale as keyof typeof track.title] || track.title.en

// ✅ GOOD - Type-safe approach
type LocaleKey = 'en' | 'es' | 'zh-TW'
const title = track.title[locale as LocaleKey] || track.title.en
```

## Translation Keys

Located in `messages/`:
- `messages/en.json`
- `messages/es.json`
- `messages/zh-TW.json`

All keys must exist in all language files.
